  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the numerator be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>, then <math> <mrow> <mtext>f</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />On differentiating w.r.t. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>, we get<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>f</mtext> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>&#183;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>x</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> <mo>-</mo> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> ...(i)<br /><br />Putting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for maxima or minima, we get,<br /><br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />Again, on differentiating w.r.t. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>, we get<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>f</mtext> <mo>&#8243;</mo> </msup> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>-</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>-</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> <mo>-</mo> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfenced> <mn>2</mn> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>x</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>4</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><mo>&there4;</mo> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is maximum at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />And at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is minimum<br /><br /><mo>&there4;</mo> Least value of <math> <mrow> <mtext>f</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br />&nbsp;"
